# Who has to approve a change, and to what.
#
# One owner, everything. `*` matches every path in the repository, so every pull request needs an
# approving review from @tuxcomputers and from nobody else -- which is the point: with branch protection
# set to require a code owner's review, an approval from anybody else does not satisfy it.
#
# **The owner is exempt, and that is deliberate rather than an oversight.** GitHub will not let somebody
# approve their own pull request, so a rule requiring one approval would leave the only person able to
# give it unable to merge anything. `enforce_admins` is off on `main` for exactly that reason, which is
# what lets the owner merge without a review while everybody else needs one.
#
# **This file only counts on the default branch.** GitHub reads CODEOWNERS from the *base* of a pull
# request, so a change to it does nothing until it is merged into `main`.

* @tuxcomputers
